n\nAs Montresor leads Fortunato deeper into the damp, bone-strewn vaults beneath the river, he feigns concern for his companion’s cough, offering wine to keep him compliant and disoriented. This calculated manipulation underscores Montresor’s cold precision and psychological control. The descent becomes increasingly oppressive, with the air thick with decay and the walls lined with human remains, symbolizing the inevitability of Fortunato’s fate. The turning point arrives when Montresor reaches a secluded niche in the catacombs—hidden and unmarked—where he chains Fortunato to the wall, revealing his true intentions with chilling calm.\n\nThe climax unfolds as Fortunato’s initial laughter gives way to desperate pleas, his cries echoing through the vaults before fading into silence. Montresor methodically begins to brick up the niche, sealing Fortunato alive within the tomb. Each stone placed is a step toward finality, a testament to Montresor’s meticulous planning and emotional detachment. The story concludes with Montresor’s haunting declaration that no one has disturbed the tomb in fifty years, a final assertion of his success and the enduring weight of his vengeance. The act is not just murder but a permanent entombment of both body and memory, a testament to the depths of Montresor’s obsession and the irreversible consequences of unchecked revenge.</div>\n                \n                <p style=\"margin-top: 1rem; color: var(--muted);\">\n                    <strong>Themes:</strong> revenge, deception, isolation\n                </p>\n                \n            </section>\n            \n\n            \n            <section>\n                <h2>🤖 Analysis Models</h2>\n                <table style=\"width: 100%; margin-top: 1rem; border-collapse: collapse;\">\n                    <thead>\n                        <tr style=\"border-bottom: 2px solid var(--primary);\">\n                            <th style=\"text-align: left; padding: 0.75rem; color: var(--mu